# Code Compete PR review

When reviewing a pull request in this repository:

1. Read `docs/10-pr-review-checklist.md` and apply it.
2. Compare the change to `docs/02-product-and-scope.md` and `docs/09-roadmap.md`. Flag work that jumps ahead of a working 1v1 match (Battle Royale, CRDT, VS Code, Magic UI, multi-region AWS, practice-site features).
3. Treat these as security blockers: sandbox network/Docker socket/host FS access, missing resource limits, hidden test leakage, IDOR, unauthenticated submit/WS, committed secrets, unbounded `code` payloads, SQL concatenation.
4. Treat these as correctness blockers: illegal match state transitions, two winners from concurrent ACs, client-side match clocks, submit outside `RUNNING`.
5. If REST/WS/events/tables change, require an update under `docs/` in the same PR.
6. Do not revive Express/Prisma/FastAPI/CDK/LeetCode GraphQL from git history unless `docs/11-open-questions.md` records that decision.
7. Cite files and explain impact. Do not nitpick landing-page aesthetics before the match loop exists.
